content.text:
### Basic useMicVAD Example

Source: https://github.com/ricky0123/vad/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/useMicVAD.md

A basic example demonstrating how to use the useMicVAD hook in a React component to create a voice recorder. It shows how to handle loading, error states, and control the VAD instance.

```typescript
import { useMicVAD } from "@ricky0123/vad-react"

export function VoiceRecorder() {
  const vad = useMicVAD({
    model: "v5",
    baseAssetPath: "/",
    onnxWASMBasePath: "/",
    onSpeechEnd: (audio) => {
      console.log("Speech segment:", audio)
      // Send to server or process locally
    },
  })

  return (
    <div>
      {vad.loading && <p>Loading VAD...</p>}
      {vad.errored && <p>Error: {vad.errored}</p>}

      {!vad.loading && !vad.errored && (
        <>
          <p>Status: {vad.listening ? "Listening" : "Stopped"}</p>
          <p>User Speaking: {vad.userSpeaking ? "Yes" : "No"}</p>

          <button onClick={vad.toggle}>
            {vad.listening ? "Stop" : "Start"}
          </button>
        </>
      )}
    </div>
  )
}
```

--------------------------------

### Configure useMicVAD Hook with Custom Options

Source: https://github.com/ricky0123/vad/blob/master/_autodocs/configuration.md

Set up the `useMicVAD` React hook with standard MicVAD options and React-specific settings like `userSpeakingThreshold`. This example shows how to manage loading, listening, and speaking states within a React component.

```typescript
import { useMicVAD } from "@ricky0123/vad-react"

function MyComponent() {
  const vad = useMicVAD({
    // Inherit all MicVAD options
    model: "v5",
    baseAssetPath: "/",
    onnxWASMBasePath: "/",
    positiveSpeechThreshold: 0.3,

    // Add React-specific option
    userSpeakingThreshold: 0.6,

    // Callbacks
    onSpeechEnd: (audio) => {
      // Handle segment
    },
  })

  return (
    <div>
      {vad.loading && <div>Loading...</div>}
      {vad.listening && <div>Listening...</div>}
      {vad.userSpeaking && <div>🔴 Speaking</div>}
    </div>
  )
}
```

--------------------------------

### Next.js VAD Component with Configuration

Source: https://github.com/ricky0123/vad/blob/master/_autodocs/QUICK_START.md

A React component for Next.js that uses `useMicVAD` and specifies custom base paths for VAD assets and ONNX WASM files.

```tsx
// components/VoiceChat.tsx
import { useMicVAD } from "@ricky0123/vad-react"

export default function VoiceChat() {
  const vad = useMicVAD({
    baseAssetPath: "/vad/",
    onnxWASMBasePath: "/onnx/",
  })

  if (vad.loading) return <p>Loading...</p>
  if (vad.errored) return <p>Error: {vad.errored}</p>

  return (
    <button onClick={vad.toggle}>
      {vad.listening ? "Stop Listening" : "Start Listening"}
    </button>
  )
}
```

--------------------------------

### Minimal VAD Example in React

Source: https://github.com/ricky0123/vad/blob/master/_autodocs/QUICK_START.md

Use the `useMicVAD` hook in React to manage VAD state and functionality. Provides a toggle button to start/stop listening.

```tsx
import { useMicVAD } from "@ricky0123/vad-react"

export function App() {
  const vad = useMicVAD({
    onSpeechEnd: (audio) => {
      console.log("Got audio:", audio)
    },
  })

  return (
